#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119488 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/id #uuid "9b2026e3-781b-5e73-8dc2-0e8f2789fe67" :question/math-academy-id "e-3065" :question/problem "Consider the curve  $\\mathbf r(t)=\\left\\langle 2t-1 ,\\: 8t+2 ,\\: -2t \\right\\rangle, \\, t \\geq 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $\\mathbf{r}(0)$ to $\\mathbf{r}(t)$ is given by $s=6\\sqrt{2}t.$ Find $\\mathbf R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since  $s=6\\sqrt{2}t,$ we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6\\sqrt{2}t & =s \\\\ t & =\\frac{s}{6\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ t & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s \\geq 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12}) \\\\  & =⟨2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})-1,\\,8(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})+2,\\,-2(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{12})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{6}-1,\\,\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}s}{6}+2,\\,-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}s}{6}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}⟨\\sqrt{2}s-6,\\,4\\sqrt{2}s+12,\\,-\\sqrt{2}s⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119489 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/id #uuid "74f33486-6391-5ec0-8a5b-bb51c9af2d55" :question/math-academy-id "e-3066" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve  $\\mathbf r(t)=2(t\\cos{t}-\\sin{t})\\,\\mathbf i+2(t\\sin{t}+\\cos{t})\\,\\mathbf j, \\, t \\geq 0$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find $\\mathbf{r}'(t)$ and its magnitude $\\|\\mathbf{r}'(t)\\|\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,i+2\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =2(\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)\\,i+2(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)\\,j \\\\  & =-2t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,i+2t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|2t|\\sqrt{(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)^{2}+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =2t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that in the last step, we removed the absolute value bars since $t>0.$ \n\nNext, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}2u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={u}^{2}{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & ={t}^{2}-0 \\\\  & ={t}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $s=t^2,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =s \\\\ t & =\\pm \\sqrt{s} \\\\ t & =\\sqrt{s},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ntaking the positive root because $t>0.$  \n\nFinally, the vector function that parametrizes $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{s}) \\\\  & =2(\\sqrt{s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s})\\,i+2(\\sqrt{s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{s}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{s})\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119490 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/id #uuid "48350682-3ad0-5311-bb47-782ec454390c" :question/math-academy-id "e-3067" :question/problem "Given the curve  $\\mathbf r(t)=\\cos{t}\\,\\mathbf i - \\sin{t}\\,\\mathbf j+\\sqrt{3}t\\,\\mathbf k, \\, t \\geq 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $\\mathbf r(0)$ to $\\mathbf r(t)$ is given by $s=2t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $\\mathbf{T}(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=2t,$ we have that $t=\\dfrac{s}{2}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $\\mathbf R(s)$ that parametrizes $\\mathbf r(t)$ by its arc length is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{2}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\sqrt{3}\\cdot \\frac{s}{2}k \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s,$ the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf T(s) = \\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}s}\\mathbf R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}s}{2})k \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\,k \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,i-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})\\,j+\\sqrt{3}\\,k).\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357849 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a8dbe34d-2147-5006-bfe6-f3c9a8614546" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "s\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357851} {:answer/id #uuid "399d0055-d73b-5947-8933-a20509452add" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357852} {:answer/id #uuid "fa11530e-1e9c-5050-a590-c308f4c08ad9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357853} {:answer/id #uuid "1b6c4c32-dfc5-52e2-af3f-84e4473941ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s+1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357854} {:answer/id #uuid "56e86d0a-0acf-5dfd-a5b6-b319be220571" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}s\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357855}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "399d0055-d73b-5947-8933-a20509452add" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357852} :answer-field/id #uuid "d99044ff-d933-5a1f-ac00-00762d7e9a75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357850}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1ce59150-0075-56ed-b6d6-42ed469b42d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-127687" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(t)=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s={e}^{t}-1.$ Given that $R(s)$ is the parametrization of the given curve by its arc length $s,$ what is the $x$-component of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s={e}^{t}-1,$ we have that $t=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1).$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s\\ge 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}⟨{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the $x$-component of $R$ is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357856 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c8796719-952e-5e57-b537-a8b76854dc9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357858} {:answer/id #uuid "24ed34d0-1a39-57a7-b4e0-3daa2cb48732" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2s),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2s)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357859} {:answer/id #uuid "68267bad-502f-5868-8e44-82d5479f4cd1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3s+2),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3s+2)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357860} {:answer/id #uuid "7b8803c2-b070-58f6-82c6-5d5ea8a7a613" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{3}),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{3})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357861} {:answer/id #uuid "ea1ff625-a895-54a3-96e6-72b2164ac234" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3s-6),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3s-6)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357862}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c8796719-952e-5e57-b537-a8b76854dc9f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357858} :answer-field/id #uuid "17bb1536-0a13-56d3-ac48-77d1af7ae8d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357857}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3223e0f6-e1e4-5997-b282-51a0c4f828e6" :question/math-academy-id "q-127689" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(t)=⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡3t,\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡3t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=6t.$ Find $R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=6t,$ we have that $t=\\frac{s}{6}.$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s,$ with $s\\ge 0,$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{6}) \\\\  & =⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{s}{6}),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot \\frac{s}{6})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,3-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357863 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9c0f3586-8d5d-5db3-af83-db5a93e055eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{6}}{6}⟨1,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357865} {:answer/id #uuid "8ff67829-40b1-5343-a9a5-4a6ce7c44a91" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=-\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨1,\\,0,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357866} {:answer/id #uuid "fafe1a90-43d7-5534-8ce7-daf3d69d4d9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨1,\\,-2,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357867} {:answer/id #uuid "328cb870-a313-5de4-9c6c-9c9e782df864" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨1,\\,-2,\\,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357868} {:answer/id #uuid "4b3aff9d-20af-5389-95a0-3788a72c6470" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨2,\\,-1,\\,-2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357869}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fafe1a90-43d7-5534-8ce7-daf3d69d4d9c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨1,\\,-2,\\,0⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357867} :answer-field/id #uuid "363ef24a-4dcc-5f06-8e59-d512be1fae8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357864}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "f6b8de62-0230-5556-8b55-9a984894af3f" :question/math-academy-id "q-127706" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨{t}^{2},\\,-2{t}^{2},\\,-2⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s={t}^{2},$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s={t}^{2},$ we have that $t=\\sqrt{s}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{s}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨{(\\sqrt{s})}^{2},\\,-2{(\\sqrt{s})}^{2},\\,-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨s,\\,-2s,\\,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parameterized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-2s),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{5}}{5}⟨1,\\,-2,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357870 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0347f90a-b450-5864-a04b-9dd37edd0f41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨2s\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,\\,3,\\,-2s\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357872} {:answer/id #uuid "faa2ec0b-129e-5a7f-84c0-e59bb143a1df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s},\\,3,\\,\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357873} {:answer/id #uuid "f985d12a-acb6-5981-9fa8-9ec843f56c10" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨2s\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s+\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s,\\,3,\\,2s\\operatorname{cos}⁡2s-\\operatorname{sin}⁡2s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357874} {:answer/id #uuid "ae984ba7-ad74-5ff5-b7b2-dd312ac56cfd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{s}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}),\\,3,\\,\\frac{s}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2})⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357875} {:answer/id #uuid "6241c011-6908-5843-bd8b-cae475ed3d43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s},\\,3,\\,-\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357876}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "faa2ec0b-129e-5a7f-84c0-e59bb143a1df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s},\\,3,\\,\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357873} :answer-field/id #uuid "c78fe31b-a1ff-5848-933a-dc5a6b44f5a4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357871}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "792ae83b-6f8e-58bb-84d1-2c821da6f452" :question/math-academy-id "q-127723" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3,\\,t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t-\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,0,\\,-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(0)}^{2}+{(-t\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}{cos}^{2}⁡t+{t}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}({cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{t}^{2}} \\\\  & =|t| \\\\  & =t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{u}^{2}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2},$ we have that $t=\\sqrt{2s}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{2s}) \\\\  & =⟨\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s},\\,3,\\,\\sqrt{2s}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\sqrt{2s}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\sqrt{2s}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357877 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "44c19ff0-9677-53d2-8b73-50b898324319" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{s+1}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357879} {:answer/id #uuid "6774dedc-fdd4-5f55-be9b-b1aa49760ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{s+1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(s+1),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s+1)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357880} {:answer/id #uuid "aeeacb70-038c-551d-b4e6-56d4a72d15d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{s}{2}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s-1)],\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s-1)]⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357881} {:answer/id #uuid "b691cd9a-7c67-541d-8d68-db83364d3b35" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{s}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s),\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\operatorname{ln}⁡s)⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357882} {:answer/id #uuid "eba30440-2828-585a-aced-8adc91cef4f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{s+1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357883}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "eba30440-2828-585a-aced-8adc91cef4f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{s+1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357883} :answer-field/id #uuid "5fe88485-d555-5d33-9b5f-a72c01952ade" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357878}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "5d60c8dc-149c-57b3-9b22-a7e5b2f8c7d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-127727" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t)⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,{e}^{t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{e}^{t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}|\\sqrt{{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}+{(\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡t-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t+{sin}^{2}⁡t+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\sqrt{2({sin}^{2}⁡t+{cos}^{2}⁡t)} \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{t}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}{e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={e}^{u}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & ={e}^{t}-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s={e}^{t}-1,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{t}-1 & =s \\\\ {e}^{t} & =s+1 \\\\ t & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)}\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)}\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-(s+1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,(s+1)\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{s+1}{\\sqrt{2}}⟨-\\operatorname{cos}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)],\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(s+1)]⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357884 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "503a8e51-4fb6-5a74-a892-f16cc48a66a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{4}⟨2s,\\,3s,\\,2-\\sqrt{3}\\,s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357886} {:answer/id #uuid "e3f35cba-4faa-53cb-9bcd-352624839530" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨2s,\\,s+6,\\,9-2s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357887} {:answer/id #uuid "fc8d43d6-fc4f-5cde-a1a7-468bf9910643" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{4}⟨3s,\\,s,\\,1-\\sqrt{6}\\,s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357888} {:answer/id #uuid "96d17c61-73d5-5e11-820a-2fff83b3da14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨s,\\,2s-3,\\,-2s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357889} {:answer/id #uuid "b6c31581-b86f-5d86-92a7-f6d7aea1ff1e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨s,\\,2s+3,\\,2s-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357890}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e3f35cba-4faa-53cb-9bcd-352624839530" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=\\frac{1}{3}⟨2s,\\,s+6,\\,9-2s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357887} :answer-field/id #uuid "7502d2e9-26c8-5157-8a94-1b5c6df7506c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357885}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "7200ea0f-6e19-5f9b-b5e1-2ce1547933fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-127739" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨{t}^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}+2,\\,3-{t}^{4}⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}({t}^{4}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{2}{t}^{4}+2),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(3-{t}^{4})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4{t}^{3},\\,2{t}^{3},\\,-4{t}^{3}⟩ \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}⟨2,\\,1,\\,-2⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =|2{t}^{3}|\\sqrt{{(2)}^{2}+{(1)}^{2}+(-2)^{2}} \\\\  & =2{t}^{3}\\sqrt{4+1+4} \\\\  & =6{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}6{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =6{\\int }_{0}^{t}{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{u}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4}$ and $t\\ge 0,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{3}{2}{t}^{4} & =s \\\\ {t}^{4} & =\\frac{2s}{3} \\\\ t & =\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}}) \\\\  & =⟨{(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{4},\\,\\frac{1}{2}{(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{4}+2,\\,3-{(\\sqrt[4]{\\frac{2s}{3}})}^{4}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2s}{3},\\,\\frac{s}{3}+2,\\,3-\\frac{2s}{3}⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}⟨2s,\\,s+6,\\,9-2s⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120212 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b07103c9-fa65-54ec-9e1c-b4200f1f6ff3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = ⟨2s, 7 + 3s, 35 + 6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117773} {:answer/id #uuid "ce8daa73-6df9-5f12-a4fa-b5c4216fbdae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = \\frac{1}{7}⟨2s, 7 - 3s, 35 + 6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117774} {:answer/id #uuid "db2cd360-5297-5102-a6b8-7799dfdce2f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = \\frac{1}{7}⟨2s, 7 + 3s, 35 + 6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117775} {:answer/id #uuid "eb67ca1a-2ae5-5677-8e21-aec2aff9639a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = ⟨2s, 7 - 3s, 35 + 6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117776} {:answer/id #uuid "3413cc0d-dc91-5426-9eb4-af27ce15a12c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = \\frac{1}{7}⟨2s, 1 - 3s, 5 + 6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117777}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ce8daa73-6df9-5f12-a4fa-b5c4216fbdae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s) = \\frac{1}{7}⟨2s, 7 - 3s, 35 + 6s⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117774} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef45a99a-4388-5437-8221-7c3fd92de1c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117772}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "cd2d22fe-d6c9-55e5-8f32-f782e37e2d9e" :question/math-academy-id "q-33860" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(t)=⟨2t,\\,1-3t,\\,5+6t⟩$, $t\\ge 0$, for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=7t.$ Find $R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=7t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{7}.$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s$, with $s\\ge 0$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{7}) \\\\  & =⟨2(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,1-3(\\frac{s}{7}),\\,5+6(\\frac{s}{7})⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{7}⟨2s,\\,7-3s,\\,35+6s⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120213 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c4a156a3-783f-5d10-b422-c497a68d4c25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s) = \\frac{4}{5}\\sin (\\frac{s}{10})i - \\frac{4}{5}\\cos (\\frac{s}{10})j + \\frac{3}{5}k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117779} {:answer/id #uuid "d4857719-2940-5346-a8a4-e8945f085695" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s) = 80\\sin (\\frac{s}{10})i - 80\\cos (\\frac{s}{10})j + \\frac{3}{5}k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117780} {:answer/id #uuid "2d81c4a8-2d2d-50a1-a49b-7d5f2500929d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s) =-\\frac{4}{5}\\sin (\\frac{s}{10})i + \\frac{4}{5}\\cos (\\frac{s}{10})j + \\frac{3}{5}k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117781} {:answer/id #uuid "7ab216cc-6fb0-5693-8416-65e96019935f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s) =-80\\sin (\\frac{s}{10})i + 80\\cos (\\frac{s}{10})j + \\frac{3}{5}k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117782} {:answer/id #uuid "7ecde1f9-3dd3-5990-81db-ddd2c538e8dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s) =-\\frac{4}{5}\\sin (10s)i + \\frac{4}{5}\\cos (10s)j + \\frac{3}{5}k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117783}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2d81c4a8-2d2d-50a1-a49b-7d5f2500929d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s) =-\\frac{4}{5}\\sin (\\frac{s}{10})i + \\frac{4}{5}\\cos (\\frac{s}{10})j + \\frac{3}{5}k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117781} :answer-field/id #uuid "4a17fa68-80c2-57a2-af07-b0a9aff63e2b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117778}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7af7c919-7113-54d4-9f83-a2e6f1bdbb45" :question/math-academy-id "q-33861" :question/problem "Given the curve  $r(t)=8\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,i+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡t\\,j+6t\\,k,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=10t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=10t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{10}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{10}) \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+6(\\frac{s}{10})k \\\\  & =8\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i+8\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{3s}{5}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\frac{s}{10})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3s}{5})k \\\\  & =-8\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i+8\\cdot \\frac{1}{10}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})i+\\frac{4}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{10})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357891 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "079bc9c8-3ad0-59b3-90f7-0ceb51660ff0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{3/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357893} {:answer/id #uuid "407142b2-7754-5bad-b5cf-773285ff7aaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{[{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{3/2}-1]}^{3/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357894} {:answer/id #uuid "c339b86e-2fc5-5341-8263-c8354747628e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{[{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{1/3}-1]}^{3/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357895} {:answer/id #uuid "135b3dce-0e08-57ec-a58e-4bc394715204" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{[{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3}-1]}^{3/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357896} {:answer/id #uuid "d54eccbe-fae6-54b8-bcd9-cc6f8c3a1903" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{[{(\\frac{s}{2}-1)}^{1/3}+1]}^{3/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357897}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "135b3dce-0e08-57ec-a58e-4bc394715204" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{[{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3}-1]}^{3/2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357896} :answer-field/id #uuid "ad9dde94-7482-513c-a495-c538b28d6001" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "1ca96ad6-d425-5ffa-9ed6-f57d8bb5900e" :question/math-academy-id "q-33978" :question/problem "Consider the curve $r(t)=3t\\,i+2{t}^{3/2}\\,j+4\\,k,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by  $s=2(1+t)^{3/2}-2.$ Given that $R(s)$ is the parameterization of the given curve by its arc length $s,$ what is the $y$-component of $R?$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=2(1+t)^{3/2}-2$, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & =2(1+t)^{3/2}-2 \\\\ s+2 & =2(1+t)^{3/2} \\\\ \\frac{s+2}{2} & =(1+t)^{3/2} \\\\ {(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3} & =1+t \\\\ t & ={(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3}-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r({(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3}-1) \\\\  & =3[{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3}-1]\\,i+2{[{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3}-1]}^{3/2}\\,j+4\\,k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, the $y$-component of $R$ is\n\n$$\n2{[{(\\frac{s}{2}+1)}^{2/3}-1]}^{3/2}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357898 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5441d5a0-e00d-522a-a4f4-255ec856a385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{4}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357900} {:answer/id #uuid "e65e3e77-6867-5041-9432-8e035867127d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{2s}{5}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357901} {:answer/id #uuid "642ee3a3-cdf3-5486-9a58-da0332b1138d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{4s}{5}\\,i+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357902} {:answer/id #uuid "02b851ff-44d4-5907-b8b6-992047ad24c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{4s}{5}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357903} {:answer/id #uuid "961e1e95-9f08-584a-9b74-b0ac2d055046" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{3}{5}\\,i+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5441d5a0-e00d-522a-a4f4-255ec856a385" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "T(s)=\\frac{4}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357900} :answer-field/id #uuid "342a7d3c-8e55-59c1-9e27-e085d5054ad0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e76e3b07-32af-5d5f-b514-7d469fcb5c34" :question/math-academy-id "q-33984" :question/problem "Given the curve $r(t)=8t\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡6t\\,j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡6t\\,k,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=10t,$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=10t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{10}.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{10}) \\\\  & =8(\\frac{s}{10})\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{6s}{10})j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{6s}{10})k \\\\  & =\\frac{4s}{5}\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4s}{5})i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5}))j+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5}))k \\\\  & =\\frac{4}{5}\\,i-\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})j+\\frac{3}{5}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3s}{5})k.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357905 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ef2c4b9b-cf73-56d1-96b1-73f48b50ed7b" :knowledge-point/title "Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length Given Its Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f3598289-8a88-581c-8e89-30113fc716e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,i+(2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357907} {:answer/id #uuid "4e145a3a-4e53-5186-942f-ae64429933cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{4}))\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357908} {:answer/id #uuid "6193b2ce-33fd-5437-8546-7655731edfd9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8s))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8s))\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357909} {:answer/id #uuid "bddbe06a-5bf2-509a-8b4a-cce1984155b9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2s))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2s))\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357910} {:answer/id #uuid "9762e169-5357-53f9-a001-b467026d0d4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357911}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9762e169-5357-53f9-a001-b467026d0d4e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357911} :answer-field/id #uuid "0251424a-85da-574d-8065-4dfb02eed548" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357906}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "81d5e17e-769f-5612-9fec-c1e89601be31" :question/math-academy-id "q-34885" :question/problem "Consider the curve$r(t)=(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t))\\,j,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by  $s=4t.$ Find $R(s),$ the parametrization of the curve by its arc length $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=4t$, we have that $t=\\frac{s}{4}.$\n\nThe vector function that pametrizes the curve $r(t)$ by its arc length $s$, with $s\\ge 0$, is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{s}{4}) \\\\  & =(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{s}{4}))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{s}{4}))\\,j \\\\  & =(1+2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,i+(2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{s}{2}))\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357912 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12ae7fc4-4e78-52a1-8ead-48ff50b47e2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357914} {:answer/id #uuid "732d0135-7339-50b7-a07f-5c5ea75e2cd7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{3},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{3},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{8}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357915} {:answer/id #uuid "3002648f-cb0e-5636-b5e5-7b785371775d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{2},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,s}{6}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357916} {:answer/id #uuid "5e866f1d-3aec-5502-b667-2f0509a861b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{4},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{4},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{8}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357917} {:answer/id #uuid "07ae0937-92e7-5926-b7de-7612f96f3361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357918}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07ae0937-92e7-5926-b7de-7612f96f3361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "R(s)=⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357918} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5886932-d86b-5c01-92e5-d07d06626310" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357913}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "adcface4-b96d-5e0e-bbea-c0d9a4855e1d" :question/math-academy-id "q-78390" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=⟨\\frac{t}{2},\\,\\frac{t}{2},\\,t⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{t}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{t}{2}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2},\\,\\frac{1}{2},\\,1⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}+{1}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{1}{4}+1} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\cdot u{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\,t\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $s=\\sqrt{\\frac{3}{2}}\\,t$,  we have that $t=\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,s.$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,s,\\,\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,s,\\,\\sqrt{\\frac{2}{3}}\\,s⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{6},\\,\\frac{\\sqrt{6}\\,s}{3}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357919 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4aecbb8b-bda3-5956-9b0f-98509330a84d" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a87cb6f-007d-5e45-94a6-60913d49464b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s)\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(s)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357921} {:answer/id #uuid "494944b7-35c9-5468-8c9f-05584b88b5e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{cos}^{4}⁡(s)\\,i+{sin}^{4}⁡(s)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357922} {:answer/id #uuid "823957b0-94bf-5820-92a7-b5d6a66cd41c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{sin}⁡({s}^{4})\\,i+\\operatorname{cos}⁡({s}^{4})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357923} {:answer/id #uuid "6207e0e1-bc28-54e7-a768-08fc30563e2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(s)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357924} {:answer/id #uuid "82dd67d1-2f08-5290-b79c-f331060c91d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡({s}^{3})\\,i-\\operatorname{sin}⁡({s}^{3})\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357925}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6207e0e1-bc28-54e7-a768-08fc30563e2d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\operatorname{cos}⁡(s)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s)\\,j" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357924} :answer-field/id #uuid "600c1893-0be2-540f-82d5-dad80d8b10b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357920}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "d899d29b-8ceb-54bb-99b6-823abccec15f" :question/math-academy-id "q-78391" :question/problem "What is the parametrization of the curve $r(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{4})\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{4})\\,j,$  $\\,t\\ge 0,$ by its arc length $s?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find ${r}^{′}(t)$ and its magnitude $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{4}))i+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{4}))j \\\\  & =-4{t}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{4})\\,i+4{t}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{4})\\,j \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{[-4{t}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({t}^{4})]}^{2}+{[4{t}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({t}^{4})]}^{2}} \\\\  & =4|t{|}^{3}\\sqrt{{sin}^{2}⁡({t}^{4})+{cos}^{2}⁡({t}^{4})} \\\\  & =4{t}^{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the arc length of the curve from $0$ to $t:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}s & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}‖{r}^{′}(u)‖\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{t}4{u}^{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & ={u}^{4}\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & ={t}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nNow, since $s={t}^{4}$, we have that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{4} & =s \\\\ t & =\\sqrt[4]{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vector function that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\sqrt[4]{s}) \\\\  & =cos\\,((\\sqrt[4]{s})^{4})\\,i+sin\\,((\\sqrt[4]{s})^{4})\\,j \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡(s)\\,i+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(s)\\,j.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d3d59b31-97b7-5a41-8a52-53d0d95c1f32" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357928} {:answer/id #uuid "054068ba-d19b-5875-bb78-e5ebf218f368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{7},\\,\\frac{3}{7},\\,\\frac{6}{7}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357929} {:answer/id #uuid "c34fa0c1-d268-59bb-bc1e-3a570ca19a7f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{5},\\,\\frac{3}{5},\\,\\frac{6}{5}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357930} {:answer/id #uuid "c63a3767-a365-5453-b7f9-1240a7beb116" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{14},\\,\\frac{3}{14},\\,\\frac{2}{7}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357931} {:answer/id #uuid "df1daf56-8357-50fb-a536-c94528975bfa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{7},\\,\\frac{2}{7},\\,\\frac{3}{7}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "054068ba-d19b-5875-bb78-e5ebf218f368" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{2}{7},\\,\\frac{3}{7},\\,\\frac{6}{7}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357929} :answer-field/id #uuid "85920172-52b0-5cb8-9c08-0898a7a3f540" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357927}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "09ea4aa1-0a7a-5472-b215-c42e362c97eb" :question/math-academy-id "q-78403" :question/problem "Given the curve  $r(t)=⟨2{e}^{t},\\,3{e}^{t},\\,6{e}^{t}⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=7({e}^{t}-1),$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=7({e}^{t}-1)$, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{s}{7} & ={e}^{t}-1 \\\\ {e}^{t} & =\\frac{s}{7}+1 \\\\ t & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{s+7}{7}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{s+7}{7})) \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{s+7}{7})},\\,3{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{s+7}{7})},\\,6{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{s+7}{7})}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2\\cdot \\frac{s+7}{7},\\,3\\cdot \\frac{s+7}{7},\\,6\\cdot \\frac{s+7}{7}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2s+14}{7},\\,\\frac{3s+21}{7},\\,\\frac{6s+42}{7}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{2s+14}{7}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{3s+21}{7}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{6s+42}{7})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{2}{7},\\,\\frac{3}{7},\\,\\frac{6}{7}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357933 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fc7343e3-fa7d-58c8-b4c7-49ef5b85110b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Unit Tangent Given the Parametrization of a Curve by Arc Length"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29e9b967-146b-521c-993c-979e258e93ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{4}{9},\\,\\frac{8}{9}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357935} {:answer/id #uuid "4fae14e1-2874-5c96-8952-ed3631bec58a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{2}{9},\\,\\frac{2\\sqrt{2}}{9}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357936} {:answer/id #uuid "b5903dfc-aa33-5b90-8f94-e34b1f1e0e2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{2}{9},\\,\\frac{1}{3}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357937} {:answer/id #uuid "7deec481-43dd-50df-8afa-4a43e2c8a6f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{18},\\,\\frac{2}{9},\\,\\frac{4}{9}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357938} {:answer/id #uuid "1fe618a2-b269-5db5-8b1b-29523b373c50" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{81},\\,\\frac{4}{81},\\,\\frac{8}{81}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "29e9b967-146b-521c-993c-979e258e93ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{4}{9},\\,\\frac{8}{9}⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357935} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5a334b8-7420-59f2-92a0-f22fa7792c33" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357934}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "56897adb-706a-5c81-8930-6f2aa15c0be7" :question/math-academy-id "q-78404" :question/problem "Given the curve  $r(t)=⟨{t}^{2},\\,4{t}^{2},\\,8{t}^{2}⟩,$ $t\\ge 0,$ for which the arc length $s$ from $r(0)$ to $r(t)$ is given by $s=9{t}^{2},$ find the corresponding unit tangent $T(s),$ parametrized by $s.$" :question/worked-solution "First, since $s=9{t}^{2}$, we have that \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{t}^{2} & =\\frac{s}{9} \\\\ t & =\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the vector function $R(s)$ that parametrizes $r(t)$ by its arc length is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R(s) & =r(\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{3}) \\\\  & =⟨{(\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{3})}^{2},\\,4{(\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{3})}^{2},\\,8{(\\frac{\\sqrt{s}}{3})}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{s}{9},\\,\\frac{4s}{9},\\,\\frac{8s}{9}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n   \n\nNow, since the curve is parametrized by its arc length $s$, the unit tangent can be found as\n\n$$\nT(s)=\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s).\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}R(s) \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{9}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{4s}{9}),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{8s}{9})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{9},\\,\\frac{4}{9},\\,\\frac{8}{9}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
